<p>Brazil’s Lucas Pinheiro Braathen won gold in the men’s giant slalom at the Winter Olympics in Milan-Cortina, earning Brazil’s first-ever Winter Olympic medal. A day earlier, Kazakhstan’s Mikhail Shaidorov took men’s figure skating gold—what The New York Times called Kazakhstan’s first Olympic gold in 32 years.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/KnKIwLLB2xxeLxgzwrLNbO0K7QKtWSF21Q1jh8QHhHRgbZsHuXvMLQA53VZryvuv9-YY5cEuUbaC_6MCM0h6oKx6fMAIXT_4hIhJnd58Jq8owVH1kolxBhBQf-m4-FSiijtTmmAnmkQa5kBdb2hbOTknk5lAoL7TgUi0ltHWLCb5VQRN-sotC1zugTQJddZrTH-dSdeovK_BZJYi_cvEGU2x0B8iztOPw4cEDexn_ou4ug' alt='Mikhail Shaidorov of Kazakhstan won the gold medal in men’s figure skating on Friday at the Winter Olympics in Milan.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Margin of victory: Braathen won the giant slalom by 0.58 seconds over Switzerland’s Marco Odermatt, according to Euronews’ race report.</li><li>Continental milestone: Several outlets described the result as South America’s first-ever Winter Olympics medal—a milestone that goes beyond Brazil alone.</li><li>Another medal chance: CBS said another Brazilian athlete, Nicole Rocha Silveira, could add to the tally when she competes in the women’s skeleton event on Saturday.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/14/world/olympics/brazil-kazakhstan-gold-medals-winter-olympics.html'>Lucas Pinheiro Braathen of Brazil and Mikhail Shaidorov of Kazakhstan Win Olympic Gold Medals</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/14/lucas-pinheiro-braathen-makes-history-for-brazil-after-winning-giant-slalom-gold-in-milano'>Lucas Pinheiro Braathen makes history for Brazil after winning giant slalom gold in Milano Cortina</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/brazil-south-america-medal-winter-olympics-giant-slalom-skeleton/'>Brazilian skier wins South America&#x27;s first-ever Winter Olympics medal</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/Uplifti